---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Frame 3b's program on two-way-lru, untimed, loaded and stepped to its end one instruction per op, as Space steps it. The load is a setup without a number or a label; each instruction's last event moves the pc, after the rank update when there is one; and access #5 reads as the design's table, into r3 (cases 7, 2, 7, 1, 4 and 3)."
---
- | setup | - | - | - | Loaded a program of 6 instructions. Registers and the pc are reset; the cache and memory keep their contents.
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x0B0: tag 0x02, set 3, offset 0 (word 0).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, compulsory | - | Set 3: no valid way holds tag 0x02. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 0 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 3/0, tag 3/0, word 3/0/0, word 3/0/1, word 3/0/2, word 3/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0B0–0x0BF from memory.
1.5 | write | writePolicy | dirty 3/0, word 3/0/0, pc | - | Write 5 into word 0 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0B0 is now stale.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x02. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 0 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
2.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
2.5 | complete | - | r1, pc | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Store 0x1A4: tag 0x06, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x06. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Way 1 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
3.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, fills | - | Fill way 1 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
3.5 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/1, word 2/1/1 | - | Write 7 into word 1 of way 1 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x1A4 is now stale.
3.6 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1, pc | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 1 becomes 0 (most recent); way 0 is 1.
4.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
4.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, loads, hits | - | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x02 matches. Hit.
4.3 | complete | - | r2 | - | Read word 2 of way 0 (66) into r2.
4.4 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1, pc | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 0 becomes 0 (most recent); way 1 is 1.
5.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x2A4: tag 0x0A, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
5.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x0A. Miss.
5.3 | victim | replacement | - | - | Way 1 chosen: least recently used (rank 1).
5.4 | writeBack | writePolicy | memory 0x1A4, writebacks | - | Way 1 is dirty: write line 0x1A0 back to memory first.
5.5 | evict | replacement | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, dirty 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x1A0 (tag 0x06) from way 1.
5.6 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, fills | - | Fill way 1 with line 0x2A0–0x2AF from memory.
5.7 | complete | - | r3 | - | Read word 1 of way 1 (68) into r3.
5.8 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1, pc | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 1 becomes 0 (most recent); way 0 is 1.
6.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x1A4: tag 0x06, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
6.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, conflict | - | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x06. Miss.
6.3 | victim | replacement | - | - | Way 0 chosen: least recently used (rank 1).
6.4 | evict | replacement | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x0A0 (tag 0x02) from way 0.
6.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
6.6 | complete | - | r4 | - | Read word 1 of way 0 (7) into r4.
6.7 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1, pc | - | LRU ranks in set 2: way 0 becomes 0 (most recent); way 1 is 1.
